msgid "What the validator says"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Every sentence of the validator and of the tools around it, with its "
"code and its level, as the library writes them.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The EM tools validate a package with one implementation: the Extensions "
"window shows its words before installing, ``python -m "
"s3dgraphy.extensions validate`` prints them, the repositories run them on"
" every proposal. Each problem has a **code**, a **level** and a sentence "
"in English and Italian (``--lang it``); the place where it was found (a "
"file, a key) is written in front of the sentence."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**error** — it refuses the package, or only its code when the problem "
"concerns the code alone (the data go in all the same);"
msgstr ""

msgid "**warning** — advice, never a refusal;"
msgstr ""

msgid "**info** — what ``build`` changed in the archive it wrote;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**refusal** — an operation of the command line or of the window that "
"stops (an installation, a repository, a removal), with the reason;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**—** — said by another path: a file that cannot be read, a signature, a "
"node's closed space."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The words between ‹ › are filled in with the case at hand: a path, a key,"
" a value, a version. ``python -m s3dgraphy.extensions validate --json`` "
"gives the same problems as data, each with its ``code``."
msgstr ""

